---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base
  title="Digits vs Xenett for bookkeeping firms — AI-native ledger vs AI review on QBO and Xero"
  description="Digits (AI-native ledger, $65-$250/client) vs Xenett (AI review on top of QuickBooks Online and Xero, $7.50-$10/client): what each automates, who keeps the ledger, and 20-client cost math. Prices verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Digits vs Xenett</h1>
  <p>These two solve the month-end problem from opposite ends. Digits replaces the client's ledger: it is an AI-native general ledger that categorizes and reconciles transactions around the clock, and firms pay per client. Xenett keeps QuickBooks Online or Xero as the ledger and adds an AI review layer that scans each client's P&amp;L and Balance Sheet for issues before you sign off, also priced per client.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/xenett`}>Xenett</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>US startup and small-business clients you can move onto a new ledger, where you want bookkeeping to run itself</td><td>Firms staying on QBO or Xero that want every client file checked for errors before review</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>Per client: Essentials $65/mo, Core $100/mo, Pro $250/mo. No seat fees; firm's own books free for partner firms; partner discounts on contract. 30-day free trial.</td><td>Per client: AI Financials Review $7.50/mo, Workflow $10/mo. Add-ons: Accruals + AI $15/client/mo, Inter-company Rec $10/client/mo ($0 for the first 60 days). Unlimited users. Enterprise by quote.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledger</td><td>Digits is the ledger (replaces QBO/Xero). US entities only.</td><td>Works on QuickBooks Online and Xero; you keep the client's existing file.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>What it automates</td><td>Categorization, continuous bank reconciliation, statement fetching, quality checks, bill pay and invoicing; Core adds automated schedules and dimensions</td><td>Review points: duplicates, GL inconsistencies, AR/AP issues, undeposited funds, uncategorized entries, missing name/class/location, custom rules; Accruals add-on covers prepaids, payroll accruals, deferred revenue, flux analysis</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Firm workflow</td><td>Checklist, roles and per-client permissions, central billing</td><td>Workflow plan: projects and tasks, time tracking, capacity planning, 1099s (US), documents, email and Drive integration</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost at 20 clients (list prices, monthly)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Xenett AI Financials Review: 20 × $7.50 = $150. Workflow: 20 × $10 = $200. Adding Accruals + AI to Workflow: 20 × $25 = $500.</li>
    <li>Digits Essentials: 20 × $65 = $1,300. Core: 20 × $100 = $2,000.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The numbers are not like for like. Xenett sits on top of a QBO or Xero subscription that you or the client still pay for; Digits includes the ledger itself, so that subscription goes away. Digits partner-firm discounts are not published. All figures before discounts or promotions.</p>

  <h2>When to choose Digits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your clients are US businesses willing to leave QBO or Xero.</li>
    <li>You want categorization and reconciliation to happen continuously, not caught at review time.</li>
    <li>You sell a fixed-fee, automation-first bookkeeping package and want one platform for it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Xenett</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your clients stay on QuickBooks Online or Xero, including clients outside the US.</li>
    <li>Your bottleneck is review quality: catching miscoded, duplicate and uncategorized entries before sign-off.</li>
    <li>You want a low per-client cost with unlimited users, or a light practice management layer at $10/client.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Sources: digits.com/pricing and xenett.com/pricing, checked 2026-10-18. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/compare/digits-alternatives`}>Digits alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/xenett-alternatives`}>Xenett alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/bank-reconciliation-tools`}>Bank reconciliation tools</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/xenett-vs-financial-cents`}>Xenett vs Financial Cents MEC</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
